{"id":"4bdb15c051f54fe0","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration.md","title":"ZFC Comp Recursive Enumeration","display":"df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration — ZFC Comp Recursive Enumeration","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration","aliases":["58-df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration"],"display":"df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration — ZFC Comp Recursive Enumeration","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[../batch07/58-df-recursive.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-comp-recursive-enumeration — ZFC Comp Recursive Enumeration"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"da0bcf2e3f060472\" href=\"?note=da0bcf2e3f060472\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-recursive.md\">../batch07/58-df-recursive.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e,A,\\Phi\\in V\">\\(e,A,\\Phi\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pRec}\">\\(\\mathrm{pRec}\\)</span> (partial-recursive function class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"da0bcf2e3f060472\" href=\"?note=da0bcf2e3f060472\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-recursive.md\">../batch07/58-df-recursive.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{pRec}_1\\coloneqq\\mathrm{pRec}\\cap(\\omega\\rightharpoonup\\omega)\">\\(\\mathrm{pRec}_1\\coloneqq\\mathrm{pRec}\\cap(\\omega\\rightharpoonup\\omega)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCompRecursiveEnumeration}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCompRecursiveEnumeration}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}comp\\text{-}recursive\\text{-}enumeration} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcCompRecursiveEnumeration}_S(e,A,\\Phi)\\leftrightarrow e\\in\\omega\\land\\Phi:\\omega\\twoheadrightarrow\\mathrm{pRec}_1\\land A=\\operatorname{ran}(\\Phi(e))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}comp\\text{-}recursive\\text{-}enumeration} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcCompRecursiveEnumeration}_S(e,A,\\Phi)\\leftrightarrow e\\in\\omega\\land\\Phi:\\omega\\twoheadrightarrow\\mathrm{pRec}_1\\land A=\\operatorname{ran}(\\Phi(e))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The numbering <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Phi\">\\(\\Phi\\)</span> is now an explicit parameter and is required to enumerate the unary partial-recursive functions; the former binary predicate depended on an undeclared global numbering <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle\\varphi_e\\rangle\">\\(\\langle\\varphi_e\\rangle\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-recursive.md","status":"resolved","id":"da0bcf2e3f060472","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-recursive.md]]","embed"